                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "For most small businesses, **HubSpot CRM** is the best starting point: it offers a capable free tier, is easy to use, and can grow into marketing, sales, and customer service tools.[1][5]\n\n| CRM | Best for | Key consideration |\n|---|---|---|\n| **HubSpot CRM** | Best overall and best free option | Strong free entry point; paid features can become expensive as you add marketing and automation.[5] |\n| **Zoho CRM** | Best value and customization | Broad functionality at a relatively affordable price; better suited to businesses willing to configure the system.[7] |\n| **Pipedrive** | Best for straightforward sales pipelines | Simple, visual deal tracking; ideal for sales-focused teams.[7] |\n| **Less Annoying CRM** | Best for simplicity | Minimal learning curve and fewer unnecessary features.[7] |\n| **Salesforce Starter** | Best for future growth | Powerful scaling option, but typically more complex than a small business needs initially; listed at $25 per user monthly.[9] |\n\n**Quick recommendation:**\n- Choose **HubSpot** if you want to start free and may add marketing or support later.\n- Choose **Pipedrive** if your main need is managing leads and sales opportunities.\n- Choose **Zoho** if price, customization, and all-in-one features matter most.\n- Choose **Less Annoying CRM** if you want the simplest possible system.\n\nBefore choosing, confirm pricing for your number of users, email integration, reporting, automation, and data export.",
